@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #0b7a75

title Asked to search: the Gate hands off, the UniversalNavigator drives the route,\nthe tools do the work, and one stream returns

start

:**Gate** (transport facade)
collects the session token, the HTTP head, and the
POST/GET parameters (each if present), and passes
them through the **UniversalNavigatorProxy** to the
UniversalNavigator. It knows nothing else;
note right #f3f4f6
  One generic gate module, no routes of its own,
  the only component that knows transport exists.
  The client arrives on the client_sessioned route.
end note

:**UniversalNavigator**, the only node that accepts
external traffic, verifies the session-token proof,
maintains the session, and takes the utterance;

:**UtteranceManager**: one model call. The cached
preamble plus every tool's registry fragment in, the
dispatch SET out. Non-blocking, and it knows no parameters;
note right #f3f4f6
  The classifier is gone; this IS the classifier.
  It answers with routes, it never commands. It also
  holds the **RequestUsersRefinement** capability, the one
  surface that ever speaks to the user, in two forms:
  RequestUsersRefinement() -- its own LLM authors the
  question when classification finds no dispatchable route
  or a missing slot; RequestUsersRefinement(question) -- a
  dispatched tool authored the question and it delivers it.
end note

:**UniversalNavigator** validates the selection
against the may_call map and drives the route;

:domain tools mine the parameter values out of the
utterance. Running in parallel: **SpecialtyFilter**
resolves the kinds of provider that treat a named
complaint, and **Geo** resolves the free-text
geography (misspellings included);
note right #f3f4f6
  Tool answers ride the passed document. The
  UniversalNavigator tracks parameter state and
  raises if two values conflict. SpecialtyFilter and
  Geo are page-scoped members of individualProvider,
  not pages; they run side by side.
end note

:**UniversalNavigator** completeness test:
compare the passed document against the search
tool's required input fields, from the live registry;
note left #f3f4f6
  The required flags in the registry are the tool's
  prerequisites. A value present but empty is not in
  force: an empty string and a missing one are the
  same absence to the person who did not say it.
end note

if (any required field unmet?) then (yes)
  :the search route needs refined input, so it calls
  **UtteranceManager.RequestUsersRefinement(question)** with
  the facts: the names of the missing fields. The
  **RequestUsersRefinement** capability inside the
  UtteranceManager authors the user-facing question;
  note right #f3f4f6
    RequestUsersRefinement is a capability of the
    UtteranceManager, not a separate tool the
    UniversalNavigator dispatches. The UtteranceManager
    decides whether an utterance is sufficient to dispatch
    to >=1 tool and dispatches if so; a route needing more
    input reaches back through RequestUsersRefinement to
    ask the user.
  end note
  :the question is authored and returned
  as an internal callback;
  :**UniversalNavigator** merges the answer, and its
  **Gate** writes the one stream as kind 'prompt';
  stop
else (no)
  :**UniversalNavigator** dispatches **ProviderSearch**
  on what the passed document holds;
  :**ProviderSearch** runs and returns the rows
  as an internal callback;
  :**UniversalNavigator** merges as the ledger entry closes
  (timeout facts race the callback), and its
  **Gate** writes the one stream;
  stop
endif

@enduml
